  {
    "id": "342:422",
    "name": "Frame 91",
    "x": 0,
    "y": 2726,
    "width": 1440,
    "height": 444,
    "texts": [
      {
        "id": "342:428",
        "text": "Problem Space",
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 205,
        "h": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "342:429",
        "text": "Today&#39;s platforms are built for engagement, not meaningful relationships. Social media allows creators to build large communities but offers little control over personal interactions, while traditional dating apps prioritize discovery at scale over trust and compatibility. This creates a gap for creators who want to build genuine connections without compromising their privacy, and for users who seek authentic interactions beyond public comments and endless swiping. InfluCrush was conceived to bridge this gap by creating a relationship platform centered around trust, intentional access, and creator control.",
        "x": 81,
        "y": 128.5,
        "w": 588,
        "h": 250
      }
    ],
    "shapes": []
  },
  {
    "id": "342:430",
    "name": "Frame 92",
    "x": 0,
    "y": 3170,
    "width": 1440,
    "height": 389,
    "texts": [
      {
        "id": "342:432",
        "text": "Key Challenges",
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 209,
        "h": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "342:433",
        "text": "For Users Meaningful conversations are difficult to initiate in crowded social platforms, while traditional dating apps often encourage superficial interactions. For Creators Managing thousands of unsolicited messages makes it challenging to identify genuine connection requests while maintaining personal boundaries. For Existing Platforms Current products solve either audience engagement or matchmaking, but neither supports structured, trust-first relationships between creators and their communities.",
        "x": 0,
        "y": 72,
        "w": 653,
        "h": 275
      }
    ],
    "shapes": []
  },
  {
